---
// promptanddone.com/anatomy — the ANATOMY pack (DM deliverable for the "anatomy-claude-machines" reel). Prepared, not deployed.
import PackLayout from '../layouts/PackLayout.astro';
const install = 'npx skills add wheresryan22/anatomy -g -a claude-code';
const prompt = '/anatomy explain how an LLM picks its next word and what temperature does, interactive. One HTML page, light theme, fits a phone screen.';
---
<PackLayout title="Anatomy: one line, a working machine — Prompt &amp; Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · ANATOMY pack</p>
      <h1>One line to Claude, a working machine</h1>
      <p class="tag">Anatomy is a free, open-source (MIT) Claude Code skill by @wheresryan22. Ask how something works and it builds an interactive figure you can drag and tap.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">1</span> Install (Claude Code)</h2><pre><code>{install}</code></pre>
      <p>Needs Node.js 20.10+ and Chrome (for its self-checks). No API keys. Also runs in Codex, OpenCode, Antigravity and MiniMax Code: see the README.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/wheresryan22/anatomy">github.com/wheresryan22/anatomy</a></p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">2</span> The exact prompt from the reel</h2><pre><code>{prompt}</code></pre>
      <p>Our run (17 Oct 2026): Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code, 6 min 40 s, $1.77 of usage at API list price. The word odds in that machine are example numbers; the softmax and temperature maths are real.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h2><span class="n">3</span> Know before you run it</h2>
      <p>It uses your Claude plan or API usage. Small figures took us minutes; big ones take much longer (a review measured about 2 hours for a mechanical watch). It draws machines and instruments, not charts or people.</p></section>
  </main>
</PackLayout>


